{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "e9035c72-0fb4-52af-890e-d4096fcec9da",
  "Description": "A cube is cut into Voronoi cells and dropped: every cell is its own convex body.\n\n[VoronoiFracture] splits the [CubeGeometry] into parts. Connected to the Geometry input of [RigidBody], each part becomes a body with a convex hull of its own. [RigidBodyGeometry] returns the same geometry with every part moved by its body, and [GeometryToMesh] compiles it for drawing.\n\nAKA: shatter, destruction, break, debris, voronoi, convex hull, geometry\n\nTips\n- The result of [RigidBodyGeometry] is ordinary geometry: put [BevelGeometry], [ExplodeGeometry] or any other geometry operator after it.\n- More points in [ScatterPointsInVolume] give more, smaller pieces.\n- Position and Rotation on the [RigidBody] move the whole object before it is released.",
